@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: one helper's exit status, under set -e, ends the whole sandbox — and how twelve wrong answers preceded the right one
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: internal/contract/seed_abort_test.go
'
' NOT THE ONLY ONE. _node_json_field had the same defect for a different reason —
' it runs `node -e`, and the cecli image ships python and no node, so it returned
' 127 into the same kind of command substitution. All 24 command-substituted
' helpers were then audited by measurement inside the image; two were non-zero and
' both are fixed. See _spec/_plans/restore-green-e2e.puml (C1) for that sweep and
' for the bare-`exec` stderr bug that hid it.
'
' ── THE DEFECT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' _node_version_file looks for .nvmrc then .node-version and, finding neither,
' falls off the end of its loop carrying the failed test's status:
'
'   _node_version_file() {
'     for f in .nvmrc .node-version; do
'       [[ -f "$d/$f" ]] && { head -n1 ...; return 0; }
'     done            <- no `return 0`: rc is the last [[ -f ]], which is 1
'   }
'
' Its caller assigns that into a variable:
'
'   want_node="$(_node_json_field "$pkg" engines.node)"
'   [[ -n "$want_node" ]] || want_node="$(_node_version_file "$scan")"
'
' and proveo-seed runs under `set -euo pipefail`. An assignment inherits its
' command substitution's status, so a workspace with no node version pin ABORTS
' THE ENTIRE STARTUP COMMAND. "Nothing found" is the ordinary case here, not an
' error — that is the whole bug, and the fix is one `return 0`.
'
' ── WHY IT LOOKED LIKE TWO DIFFERENT BUGS ──────────────────────────────────
' The abort lands wherever the seed happens to be when it reaches that line, and
' what precedes it is workspace-dependent:
'
'   package.json, NO go.mod   the seed reaches the node block within a second,
'                             aborts before the agent session opens, and sbx
'                             reports "failed to run sandbox container" — no
'                             sandbox at all.
'   package.json AND go.mod   the Go block runs first (_install_go, then
'                             `go install gopls@latest`), which takes ~15-20s.
'                             The container is up and the AGENT IS LIVE by the
'                             time the abort happens, so it presents as the agent
'                             dying at ~17s with no message.
'
' Same line, same status, two symptoms. The second is the one that cost a night.
'
' ── WHY ONE REPO DIED AND ANOTHER RAN FOR HOURS ────────────────────────────
' `engines.node` short-circuits the `||`, so the broken helper is never called:
'
'   pluvo/monorepo    engines.node "22.x"   never reached the bug   9560s · 9806s · 28923s
'   proveo/sandbox    engines.node absent   reached it every time   16-21s x 14
'
' Neither repo has .nvmrc or .node-version. The difference is one field in one
' package.json, which is why the failure looked like a property of the workspace
' and resisted every explanation built on timing.
'
' ── THE REPRO ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Three lines. No proveo CLI, no kit, no memory limit, one mount:
'
'   sbx run --name x -t proveo/claudecode:local \
'     -e PROVEO_WORKDIR=<repo> \
'     claude <repo>
'
' Dies at ~17s. Drop the one -e and the same sandbox runs for 40+ minutes;
' PROVEO_WORKDIR is what points _proveo_scan_root at the checkout, and nothing
' scans it without that. `-e PROVEO_AUTO_INSTALL_TOOLS=false` also fixes it,
' because that knob gates the function containing the bug.
'
' ── WHAT THIS COST, AND THE METHOD THAT ACTUALLY WORKED ────────────────────
' Twelve mechanisms were proposed and eliminated before the bisect: unsolicited
' terminal reports, config written under a live agent, the seed's exit killing its
' process group, the gopls compile, host memory, the CPU share, the browser image,
' Claude Code's failing auto-updater, MCP_GATEWAY_URL="", the model ids, the git
' identity vars, and the extra workspace mounts. Every one was argued from
' timestamps and every one was wrong.
'
' What worked was differential runs with the baseline RE-CONFIRMED between splits.
' Two things that nearly wrecked it, both worth remembering:
'   * a two-hour stretch of bisecting without re-running the baseline, during
'     which the reproducer had gone intermittent and several splits were void;
'   * "lived"/"died" read off the terminal instead of sandboxd's own
'     agent/session duration_ms — three results were misread that way, in both
'     directions.
' The harness that finally settled it refuses to start while another sandbox is
' running, and reports the verdict from the daemon log rather than the screen.
title The seed's node-version lookup — one exit status ends the sandbox

participant "sbx\nENTRYPOINT" as SBX <<cloud>>
participant "proveo-seed\nset -euo pipefail" as SEED <<app>>
participant "ensure_project_tools\n(go block: ~15-20s)" as GO <<app>>
participant "ensure_node_toolchain\nwant_node=$(_node_version_file)" as NODE <<error>>
participant "Claude Code\nagent session" as AGENT <<app>>

SBX ARROW_MAIN SEED : PROVEO_WORKDIR points _proveo_scan_root at the checkout
SEED ARROW_MAIN GO : go.mod present
SBX ARROW_QUEUE AGENT : session opens ~2s in, without waiting
GO ARROW_MAIN NODE : package.json present
NODE ARROW_ERROR SEED : rc=1 on "no version file"
SEED ARROW_ERROR AGENT : set -e aborts the startup command;\nthe live session goes with it

note over NODE
  **"Nothing found" is not a failure.** A workspace with no
  ""\.nvmrc"", no ""\.node-version"" and no ""engines\.node"" is the
  ordinary case. Reporting it as non-zero is only harmless
  until someone assigns it under ""set -e"" — which the caller
  one line up does.

  ""_lsp_custom_install"" and ""_mise_install"" also return
  non-zero here, and are LEFT ALONE: theirs are real failures
  (unsupported language, installer error) and neither is
  assigned in a command substitution.
end note

note over SEED
  **The blast radius is the whole startup command.** Not a
  warning, not a skipped step — sbx sees the startup command
  exit non-zero and tears the sandbox down. The operator is
  told "sandbox was stopped", which reads as infrastructure
  and sends them into ""sbx exec"" after a cause that was never
  in there.

  ""internal/contract/seed_abort_test\.go"" pins both halves:
  the helper returns 0 on absence, and the caller's two lines
  survive ""set -euo pipefail"" against a package.json with no
  ""engines\.node"".
end note
@enduml
